        },
        {
          "id": 1710245867,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "This works for attached example but is flawed because it will set the device protocol to first interface found. The main use case for all-zero device class/subclass/protocol in device descriptor is to have composite device (i.e. device with more than one interface).\n\nI started some tinkering to register the bluetooth dissector for the interface class and found out that the `usb_conv_info` members are updated during its lifetime in a way that messes up hci_usb dissector session id calculation. This requires some more investigation as it is not immediately clear how to fix it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6496125,
            "username": "desowin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tomasz Moń",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e423f0a8da1eede7f89748e5142d6915e4a636399964d35d888ed95ca85e2b50?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/desowin"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-12-30T19:45:19.037Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-12-30T20:01:01.883Z",
          "system": false,
